# shellcheck shell=bash
# UAT.2 cluster settings that are not versions: the ports each hub exposes,
# its API server NodePort range, and the UAT CA. Sourced by bootstrap.sh and
# check.sh. README.md explains each choice.
#
# Who creates the exposing objects (owner decisions, 2026-10-06):
#   - DMZ: uat/hub/dmz (UAT.3a) owns the Envoy and bus Services, made from
#     the chart values with pinned node ports. uat/k0s creates none.
#   - Core: 443 (and, as in UAT.3b's PR #132, 5405) are hostPorts on UAT.3b's
#     edge proxy. Core exposes no node port (its node-port mode is dropped).
# uat/k0s only sets each cluster's range and checks that nothing else is
# exposed (check.sh).

# The API server's NodePort range on each hub. Owner decisions, 2026-10-06:
# DMZ node ports 8442 (bus) and 8443 (Envoy), range 8442-8443 only; core
# range 30000-32767 (Kubernetes' default). Neither range holds a port k0s
# uses (bootstrap.sh warns if one ever does), and bootstrap.sh refuses a
# hub hostPort inside its hub's range.
UAT_DMZ_NODE_PORT_RANGE=8442-8443
UAT_CORE_NODE_PORT_RANGE=30000-32767

# Ports k0s or the node itself listen on. bootstrap.sh refuses a hub port
# that is one of them and warns when a hub's NodePort range contains one:
# 6443 API server, 8080 kube-router metrics, 8132/8133 konnectivity, 9443 k0s
# API, 10249/10250/10256 kube-proxy metrics, kubelet, kube-proxy health.
UAT_RESERVED_NODE_PORTS="6443 8080 8132 8133 9443 10249 10250 10256"

# DMZ hub (deploy/helm/nats), node ports.
# Envoy, which sprouts and the runner reach (owner decision: 8443). The
# chart's Service port is envoy.service.port (443); the pod listens on
# envoy.listenerPort (8443).
UAT_DMZ_ENVOY_PORT=8443
# The bus client port core dials (owner decision: node port 8442; the bus
# itself listens on bus.ports.client, 5406, farmer's farmerbusurl).
UAT_DMZ_BUS_PORT=8442

# Core hub (deploy/helm/farmer, Keycloak), hostPorts on UAT.3b's edge.
# 443: saasapi and Keycloak behind the edge's TLS front. 5405:
# farmer's API (farmer.apiPort), which the DMZ's Envoy dials for /v1/enroll,
# /v1/refresh, /files/ and the JWKS.
UAT_CORE_HTTPS_PORT=443
UAT_CORE_FARMER_API_PORT=5405

# Kubernetes API port on each hub (the Bastion kube tunnel's remote port).
UAT_KUBE_API_PORT=6443

# The per-run UAT CA: a cert-manager CA ClusterIssuer of this name on each
# hub, backed by a kubernetes.io/tls Secret of this name in the cert-manager
# namespace. The same root on both hubs.
UAT_CLUSTER_ISSUER=imas-uat-ca
# The Azure Private DNS zone of the run (uat/tofu private_dns_zone). The hubs'
# private names are dmz.<zone> and core.<zone>; write_endpoints puts them in
# endpoints.json under both key forms the hub scripts read. A top-level
# private_dns_zone in the uat JSON, when present, wins.
UAT_PRIVATE_DNS_ZONE=uat.imas.internal
UAT_CA_SECRET=imas-uat-ca
UAT_CERT_MANAGER_NAMESPACE=cert-manager
UAT_CA_DAYS=7
